  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>odephas3</keyword>
  <short_description>Three-dimensional phase-plane ODE output function.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>status = odephas3(t, y, flag)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p>
      <b>odephas3</b> plots the first three solution components as a three-dimensional phase trajectory while an ODE solver is running.</p>
    <table style="width:100%">
  <tr><th>Flag</th><th>When called</th><th>Return value</th></tr>
  <tr><td><b>'init'</b></td><td>Before integration output starts.</td><td><b>0</b> or <b>false</b> to continue.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>''</b></td><td>At accepted output points.</td><td><b>0</b> or <b>false</b> to continue; <b>1</b> or <b>true</b> stops integration.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>'done'</b></td><td>After integration finishes.</td><td>Return value is ignored.</td></tr>
</table>
    <p>The function accepts the output callback protocol with <b>flag</b> equal to <b>'init'</b>, <b>''</b>, or <b>'done'</b>. It returns <b>0</b> to continue integration.</p>
  </description>
